An opt-in to 16.04 should be possible "soon", however the version of GDAL in 16.04 is not 2.x: http://packages.ubuntu.com/xenial/libgdal-dev.

To get the R package sf to work, an installer for sf could be created in shinyapps-package-dependencies <https://github.com/rstudio/shinyapps-package-dependencies> that downloaded the source of GDAL 2.x, compiled, and installed.

